     SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

     Every value here was read off the running stock ROM, from
     work/device_dump/display/dumpsys-display.txt, rather than copied from
     another device. The relevant line is the DisplayDeviceInfo for
     "Built-in Screen".

     Nothing panel specific belongs in this file. The panel is dual sourced
     (BOE nt36536e / CSOT nt36536) and is selected by the bootloader on the
     kernel command line, resolved inside the prebuilt dtbo. Both suppliers run
     the same mode list, so these values hold for either one.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- The panel runs 30/60/90/120/144.

         ⚠️ config_defaultRefreshRate was 60 here, on the reasoning that 60 is
         "the rate the display settles to when nothing is driving it". That
         reasoning was inferred from an idle renderFrameRate reading rather than
         read off the resource, and it is wrong. DisplayModeDirector on the
         running stock ROM reports

             mDefaultRefreshRate: 144.0
             mDefaultPeakRefreshRate: 240.0

         mDefaultRefreshRate is R.integer.config_defaultRefreshRate, so stock
         sets it to 144 (via FrameworksResTarget_Vendor.apk, the vendor RRO this
         port replaces). At 60 it posts a PRIORITY_DEFAULT_RENDER_FRAME_RATE
         vote (DisplayModeDirector.java:1225-1227) that caps the render frame
         rate globally at 60 — on a 144 Hz panel.

         config_defaultPeakRefreshRate stays 144: it is a ceiling, and the panel
         cannot exceed it anyway, so 144 and stock's 240 are equivalent here. -->
    <integer name="config_defaultPeakRefreshRate">144</integer>
    <integer name="config_defaultRefreshRate">144</integer>

    <!-- Rounded display corners, 45 px at all four positions, measured with
         dumpsys display on the running stock ROM. Stock gets this from the same
         vendor RRO as config_defaultRefreshRate above; ro.sf.rounded_corner_radius
         is unset on this device, so without an override here SystemUI would not
         mask the corners at all. -->
    <dimen name="rounded_corner_radius">45px</dimen>

    <!-- brightnessMinimum 0.0 / brightnessMaximum 1.0 /
         brightnessDefault 0.39763778 -->
    <item name="config_screenBrightnessSettingMinimumFloat" format="float" type="dimen">0.0</item>
    <item name="config_screenBrightnessSettingMaximumFloat" format="float" type="dimen">1.0</item>
    <item name="config_screenBrightnessSettingDefaultFloat" format="float" type="dimen">0.39763778</item>

    <!-- ⚠️ There used to be a config_screenBrightnessDozeFloat of 0.05 here.
         That was a misread of the dump: 0.05 is the *dim* value, not the doze
         value. Checked again on the running device:
             mScreenBrightnessDozeConfig=0.0
             mScreenBrightnessDimConfig=0.05
         Both already match AOSP's defaults (frameworks/base/core/res/res/
         values/config.xml: doze 0.0, dim 0.05), so neither needs an override
         and writing the dim value into the doze resource only made AOD wrong. -->

    <!-- No config_mainBuiltInDisplayCutout override: the panel has no cutout and
         AOSP's default for that resource is already the empty string
         (frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml). Restating it added
         nothing, and this file's stated policy is to record measured
         differences, not to copy framework-res. -->

    <!-- The device is a tablet with no notification LED and no physical
         navigation keys; both are AOSP defaults already, so they are not
         restated here. Add entries only when the stock dump disagrees with
         AOSP, so this file stays a record of measured differences rather than
         a copy of framework-res. -->
</resources>
